The XAR writer ends an archive with its heap, without the first bytes of the compressed TOC.

One of this project's patches to libarchive, which every build (macOS, Linux and
Windows) applies with patch_libarchive (native/build-config.sh), to the libarchive
release pinned there, in the order that LIBARCHIVE_PATCHES there lists them. A build
fails if any hunk does not apply exactly (no fuzz), and scripts/check-native-updates.sh
will not propose a libarchive release that it does not apply to. See "The libarchive
patches" in native/BUILD.md.

The XAR writer (archive_write_set_format_xar.c) keeps the heap, the extended
attributes and data of the files, in a temporary file until the archive is closed.
The heap starts with the checksum of the TOC, so the writer leaves room for it at the
start of that file, as many bytes as the checksum has (20 for SHA-1, the default), and
temp_offset, the end of what it has written there, starts after that room. make_toc()
then writes the compressed TOC to the same file, after the heap. xar_close() takes
length, which it calls "the length of all file extended attributes and contents",
from temp_offset before make_toc() runs, and copies length bytes out from the end of
the room. length counts the room too, so the copy took as many bytes too many as the
checksum has: every XAR archive that the writer wrote ended with the first 20 bytes of
its compressed TOC, which no item of the heap holds. Readers, libarchive's and xar's,
ignore them, as they read the heap by the offsets and lengths that the TOC gives. With
toc-checksum=none the writer leaves no room, the checksum has no bytes, and the copy
was already exact.

xar_close() now copies length less the size of the checksum, so an archive ends where
the last item of its heap ends.

libarchive 3.8.11 and libarchive's master branch (0fdf26e5, 22 November 2026) have the
old copy, which came with the writer (b7115a7d, "Add xar writer", May 2010).

The change is marked LIBARCHIVE_NET_XAR_HEAP_LENGTH, the marker that
LIBARCHIVE_PATCHES gives this patch: patch_libarchive checks that every file the patch
changes has it.

--- a/libarchive/archive_write_set_format_xar.c
+++ b/libarchive/archive_write_set_format_xar.c
@@ -1960,8 +1960,14 @@
 
 	/*
 	 * Write all file extended attributes and contents.
+	 *
+	 * LIBARCHIVE_NET_XAR_HEAP_LENGTH: they follow the room kept for
+	 * the checksum of the TOC at the start of the temporary file, so
+	 * they are that much shorter than temp_offset; copying all of
+	 * temp_offset added the first bytes of the compressed TOC, which
+	 * make_toc() writes after them, to the end of the archive.
 	 */
-	r = copy_out(a, xar->toc.a_sum.len, length);
+	r = copy_out(a, xar->toc.a_sum.len, length - xar->toc.a_sum.len);
 	if (r != ARCHIVE_OK)
 		return (r);
 	r = flush_wbuff(a);
